  "gaps": [
    "The listed Global Campus Foundations courses are the university-wide standard sequence (33 credits), and the capture states courses may be substituted. The program-level Foundations requirement is printed as \"*33 credits\".",
    "The capture says 6 credits from the major (PSY 101 and MAT 232, marked *) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements. It does not say which two Foundations courses they replace. Because of this overlap, the line items sum to 126 credits, while the printed total is 120.",
    "Title of PSY 361, the alternative to PSY 350, is not printed in the capture.",
    "GEN 101 (3 credits) is scheduled first and counts toward electives. GEN 104 (3 credits) counts toward electives for students transferring fewer than 30 credits. The capture does not break down how the 54 elective credits are reduced by these courses.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University, but no specific courses are designated as institution-only.",
    "Upper-division: a minimum of 30 upper-division credits is required, including 18 upper-division credits in the major. The capture does not identify which elective credits must be upper-division.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University.",
    "Quantitative Reasoning requirement placement (MAT 222 vs MAT 232) for this program is not explicitly stated."
  ],
